  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_budge_cb20c37db8ca85e1b9a489811ec4838b64957918ebbd78b29dfe018c6e403974f2">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>a lamb's skin with the fur dressed outward (OED s.v. budge sb.1) | a lamb's skin with the fur dressed outward (OED s.v. budge sb.1) (see also pellis bogee) | budge, a lamb's skin with the fur dressed outward (OED s.v. budge sb.1) | a lamb's skin with the fur dressed outward (OED s.v. budge sb.1) (see also pellis) | a lamb’s skin with the fur dressed outward (OED s.v. budge sb.1) | some kind of small fur used for lining garments (OED s.v. Romany^2); in the early 16^th century fine Spanish and Lombard lambskins (Veale 217) | a kind of fur, consisting of lamb’s skin with the wool dressed outwards (OED budge, n.^1), here white in color, tawed | a lamb's skin with the fur dressed outward (OED s.v. budge n.1) | a lamb’s skin with the fur dressed outward (OED s.v. budge n.1) | a kind of fur, consisting of lamb’s skin with the wool dressed outwards (OED budge, n.1) | (bodge) black in color, tawed | (bodgye pols) fur from the head and shoulders of budge (Veale 221) | a lamb's skin with the fur dressed outward (OED s.v. budge sb.1) (see also pellis bodge) | budge, a kind of fur, namely a lamb's skin with the fur dressed outward (OED budge n1) | meaning unknown | small pieces of budge | a lamb's skin with the fur dressed outward (OED s.v. budge sb.1) (see also pellis boge) | budge, a kind of fur, namely a lamb's skin with the fur dressed outward (OED budge n1), here made of the skins from the legs of the animal (Veale 217) | by characteristic | by color | by place of origin</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
